From f56d53dcfb54f24a24dd0b74466c172e922062fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:00:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] udev: fix the usb_gadget rule and match android_usb on
 the event's state

Two problems in 90-storaged.rules.

The usb_gadget rule passes the gadget's G_* variables to storage.sh with
$ENV{...}. udev's substitution is $env{...}, lower case, and it rejects
the rule:

  90-storaged.rules:20 Invalid value "/etc/udev/scripts/storage.sh
  $ENV{G_ACTION} ..." for RUN (char 30: invalid substitution type), ignoring.

udevd logs this on every start and every rules reload, and "udevadm
verify" fails the file. Use $env{}; with it the file verifies clean.

The android_usb rules matched ATTR{state}, which udev reads from sysfs
when it processes the event, not the state the event reports. A cable
plug makes the gadget send several change uevents back to back; on the
FuriLabs FLX1s (radon, configfs gadget with CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_UEVENT)
a soft reconnect sends

  DISCONNECTED, CONNECTED, DISCONNECTED, CONNECTED, CONFIGURED

and by the time udev ran the rules for the first CONNECTED, the attribute
already read DISCONNECTED again, so storage.sh told storaged
"connected": false for an event that said CONNECTED: three "false" calls
and one "true" for one reconnect. Match ENV{USB_STATE}, which both the
configfs gadget (configfs.c) and the older android.c gadget put in every
uevent they send. The same reconnect then gives one "false" per
DISCONNECTED and one "true" for CONFIGURED, each for the event that
carried it.

The udc rules are unchanged. On radon they never fire: its mtu3 UDC
sends no USB_STATE uevents, so the android_usb rules are the ones that
report the cable.

Tested on radon (LuneOS, kernel 4.19.325) with the rules file edited in
place, "udevadm control --reload" and the cable replugged in software
through /sys/class/udc/usb0/soft_connect, watching "udevadm monitor"
and storaged's journal. Before: rule 20 rejected, false/false/false/true.
After: "udevadm verify" passes, false (unplug), false, true (replug),
each matching a DISCONNECTED or CONFIGURED uevent, and the gadget ends
up configured with storaged at plugin=1.

Also tested on hammerhead (LuneOS, kernel 3.4.0, the older android.c
gadget) with the cable pulled and replugged by hand: the old rules gave
false, false, true, true, true for one replug (a DISCONNECTED and a
CONNECTED uevent processed after the attribute read CONFIGURED); the new
ones give false, false, true, one per DISCONNECTED or CONFIGURED uevent.
After a reboot udevd no longer reports line 20 as invalid.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/webOS-ports/storaged/pull/15]
---
 files/conf/90-storaged.rules.in | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/files/conf/90-storaged.rules.in b/files/conf/90-storaged.rules.in
index 4bfa60f..3adfbbd 100644
--- a/files/conf/90-storaged.rules.in
+++ b/files/conf/90-storaged.rules.in
@@ -17,9 +17,9 @@
 # LICENSE@@@
 
 
-KERNEL=="usb_gadget", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="usb_gadget", ENV{G_SUBSYSTEM}=="storage", ACTION=="change", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh $ENV{G_ACTION} $ENV{G_MEDIA_LOADED}$ENV{G_HOST_CONNECTED}$ENV{G_MEDIA_REQUESTED}$ENV{G_BUS_SUSPENDED}"
-SUBSYSTEM=="android_usb", ACTION=="change", ATTR{state}=="CONFIGURED", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh HOST_STATE_CHANGED 1"
-SUBSYSTEM=="android_usb", ACTION=="change", ATTR{state}=="DISCONNECTED", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh HOST_STATE_CHANGED 0"
+KERNEL=="usb_gadget", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="usb_gadget", ENV{G_SUBSYSTEM}=="storage", ACTION=="change", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh $env{G_ACTION} $env{G_MEDIA_LOADED}$env{G_HOST_CONNECTED}$env{G_MEDIA_REQUESTED}$env{G_BUS_SUSPENDED}"
+SUBSYSTEM=="android_usb", ACTION=="change", ENV{USB_STATE}=="CONFIGURED", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh HOST_STATE_CHANGED 1"
+SUBSYSTEM=="android_usb", ACTION=="change", ENV{USB_STATE}=="DISCONNECTED", RUN+="@WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR@/udev/scripts/storage.sh HOST_STATE_CHANGED 0"
 
 # configfs/libcomposite gadgets (Halium 9+ and mainline kernels): the UDC
 # emits change uevents carrying USB_STATE on cable and enumeration changes.
